/-!
# Phase transitions with prescribed order parameters (Georgii §16.3)

Georgii's §16.3 produces potentials `Φ ∈ ℬ_Θ` whose shift-invariant Gibbs measures are told apart
by the expectations of a prescribed finite family `f₁, …, f_N` of bounded local observables — an
*order parameter* for `Φ`. Throughout, `S = ℤ^d` is spelled `ι → ℤ` for a finite type `ι`, `λ` is
an a priori probability measure `ν` on `E`, `𝓘 = invariantEvents Θ` is the invariant σ-algebra
(14.2), `𝓟_Θ = invariantFields Θ` (14.1) and `𝒢_Θ(γ) = invariantG γ Θ` (14.14).

## Main definitions

* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.withOne`, `observableVector`, `observableMatrix`: Georgii's
  convention `f₀ = 1` and the matrix `(μ_m(f_n))_{0 ≤ m,n ≤ N}` of **Definition (16.18)**.
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.IsDiscriminating P f`: **Definition (16.18)**, `{f₁, …, f_N}` is a
  *discriminating system* for the family `P` of random fields. Georgii's `Φ ≪ {f₁, …, f_N}` is
  `IsDiscriminating (𝒢_Θ(Φ)) f`.
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.combo f a`: Georgii's `f_a = ∑ a_n f_n`.
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.HasNondegenerateInvariantMeans Θ μ f`: condition **(16.20)(ii)**,
  `μ(f_a)² < μ(μ(f_a | 𝓘)²)` for every `a ≠ 0`; `invariantVariance Θ μ f a` is the difference of
  the two sides, a quadratic form in `a`.
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.pairVolume Λ₀ i` = `Λ_i = Λ₀ ∪ (Λ₀ − i)`,
  `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.localPotentialB Λ g` = `Φ^{(Λ,g)}` of Lemma (16.10) as an element of
  `ℬ_Θ`, and `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.BThetaOrder Λ₀ f I` = **Georgii's `ℬ_Θ(f₁, …, f_N)`**
  (§16.3, before Theorem (16.21)) in his own "more precise" description, the closed linear span of
  the potentials `Φ^{(Λ₀, f_n)}` and `Φ^{(Λ_i, f_m (f_n ∘ θ_i))}`, `i ∈ I`. Taking `I = {0}ᶜ`
  gives Georgii's space; a general `I` gives his `ℬ^R_Θ` of Comment (16.24)(1) and his `ℬ^I_Θ(f)`
  of Theorem (16.30).
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.BThetaOrderNeg Λ₀ f I` = **Georgii's `ℬ⁻_Θ(f)`** of Comment
  (16.24)(2) for a single observable: the closed convex cone (a `PointedCone ℝ`) generated by
  `±Φ^{(Λ₀,f)}` and the *negatives* `−Φ^{(Λ_i, f (f ∘ θ_i))}`, `i ∈ I`.
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.correlation f μ i = μ(f · f ∘ θ_i)` and
  `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.IsOscillating I f μ`: **display (16.29)**, `μ` is
  *`f`-`I`-oscillating*.
* `Potential.BTheta.invariantFieldsOfFiniteEntropy` (in `Specification/PhaseTransition.lean`):
  Georgii's `𝓟^λ_Θ(Ω, 𝓕)`, introduced at the beginning of §16.2.

## Main results

* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.isDiscriminating_iff_span_eq_top`: **Definition (16.18)**, in the
  equivalent form used throughout — `{f₁, …, f_N}` discriminates `P` iff the vectors
  `(μ(f₀), …, μ(f_N))`, `μ ∈ P`, span `ℝ^{N+1}`.
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.isDiscriminating_invariantG_iff`: **Lemma (16.20)**,
  `Φ ≪ {f₁, …, f_N}` iff some `μ ∈ 𝒢_Θ(Φ)` has nondegenerate invariant means. Stated for an
  arbitrary specification `γ` and an arbitrary countable transformation group `Θ` moving every
  finite volume off itself, since that is all the proof uses (Theorems (14.5)(b), (14.15)(b)).
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.correlation_sub_sq_le`: **display (16.22)**;
  `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.hasNondegenerateInvariantMeans_of_specificEnergy_le`: **display
  (16.23)** — the nondegeneracy of the invariant means transfers from `μ` to any `ν` with
  `⟨ν, Ψ⟩ ≤ ⟨μ, Ψ⟩ + ε ‖Ψ‖₀` on `ℬ_Θ(f₁, …, f_N)`, provided `4ε|Λ₀| ‖f_a‖²` stays below the
  variance of `μ(f_a | 𝓘)`.
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.isDiscriminating_extremePoints_invariantG` and
  `le_encard_extremePoints_invariantG_of_isDiscriminating`: **Comment (16.19)**, a discriminating
  system for `𝒢_Θ(Φ)` already discriminates `ex 𝒢_Θ(Φ)`, so `|ex 𝒢_Θ(Φ)| ≥ N + 1`.
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.exists_pos_forall_exists_isDiscriminating`: **Theorem (16.21)**, the
  common core of (a) and (b);
  `exists_isDiscriminating_of_isDiscriminating_invariantFieldsOfFiniteEntropy` and
  `exists_isDiscriminating_and_le_encard_extremePoints` are **(16.21)(a)** (the latter with the
  "In particular `|ex 𝒢_Θ(Φ)| ≥ N + 1`" clause), and
  `exists_pos_forall_exists_isDiscriminating_norm_sub_lt` is **(16.21)(b)**. All are stated for an
  arbitrary index set `I` with finite complement, which is **Comment (16.24)(1)**: the interaction
  terms attached to any prescribed finite set of volumes `Λ_i` may be required to vanish, so the
  phase-transition potential can be forced to have arbitrarily long range
  (`exists_isDiscriminating_of_finite_excluded`).
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.exists_pos_forall_exists_isDiscriminating_neg`: **Comment
  (16.24)(2)**, Theorem (16.21) for a single observable with `ℬ_Θ(f)` replaced by the
  ferromagnetic cone `ℬ⁻_Θ(f)`. The core theorem
  `exists_pos_forall_exists_isDiscriminating` is stated for an arbitrary closed convex cone `C`
  with vertex `0` containing Georgii's test potentials `Ψ⁰`, `Ψ̄⁰` and `Ψ^i`, which is what makes
  both `ℬ_Θ(f₁, …, f_N)` and `ℬ⁻_Θ(f)` instances of it; the `ℬ_Θ(f₁, …, f_N)` instance is
  `exists_pos_forall_exists_isDiscriminating_BThetaOrder`.
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.gasObservable`, `isDiscriminating_gasObservable` and
  `exists_isDiscriminating_gasObservable`: **Example (16.25)(1)**, the lattice gas on
  `E = {0, …, N}` with `f_n = 1_{σ₀ = n}`. The `N + 1` Dirac measures at the constant
  configurations give a matrix of expectations of full rank, so every `Φ⁰ ∈ ℬ_Θ` can be modified
  inside `ℬ_Θ(f₁, …, f_N)` — outside any prescribed finite set of volumes — into a potential with
  at least `N + 1` extreme shift-invariant Gibbs measures.
* `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.exists_mem_invariantG_isOscillating`: **Theorem (16.30)**, the main
  assertion — every `Φ⁰ ∈ ℬ_Θ` can be modified inside `ℬ^I_Θ(f)` into a potential admitting an
  `f`-`I`-oscillating shift-invariant Gibbs measure.
* Auxiliary results of independent interest: `sum_smul_mem_invariantG` and
  `sum_smul_mem_invariantFields` (`𝒢_Θ(γ)` and `𝓟_Θ` are convex, `n`-ary form),
  `cond_mem_invariantG` (conditioning a `Θ`-invariant Gibbs measure on an invariant event of
  positive probability), `specificEntropy_finsetSum_smul_ne_bot` (a finite mixture of random
  fields of finite specific entropy has finite specific entropy),
  `exists_mem_invariantG_specificEnergy_le` (Proposition (16.7) read through Theorems (16.13)
  and (16.14)), and `sq_integral_lt_integral_sq_condExp_iff` (Georgii's inequality (16.20)(ii)
  is the positivity of a variance).

## Deviations from Georgii

* **(16.20)(ii)** is stated for `a ≠ 0` rather than `|a| = 1`. Both sides of the inequality are
  homogeneous of degree `2` in `a`, so the conditions are equivalent, and `a ≠ 0` avoids choosing
  a norm on `ℝ^N`.
* The proof of **(16.20)(ii) ⇒ (i)** given here is not Georgii's. Instead of approximating the
  countably generated σ-algebra `σ(f̃₁, …, f̃_N) ⊆ 𝓘` by finite subalgebras, it observes that the
  conditional measures `μ(· | A)`, `A ∈ 𝓘`, already exhaust the linear span in question.
* **`ℬ_Θ(f₁, …, f_N)`** is *defined* as the closed linear span of the potentials `Φ^{(Λ₀, f_n)}`
  and `Φ^{(Λ_i, f_m (f_n ∘ θ_i))}`, which is Georgii's own "more precise" description of the space
  he introduces by three conditions on the interaction terms. That the two descriptions agree —
  Georgii's "it is easily seen" — is
  `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.BThetaOrderCond_eq_BThetaOrder` in
  `GibbsMeasure/Specification/OrderParameterSpace.lean`, with the membership criterion
  `MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.mem_BThetaOrder_iff`.
* In the proof of **Theorem (16.30)** Georgii asks that the two sides of (16.29) differ by more
  than `2ε|Λ₀| ‖f‖²`; the correct constant is `4ε|Λ₀| ‖f‖²`, because each of the `limsup` and the
  `liminf` can move by `2ε|Λ₀| ‖f‖²`. The statement of (16.30) is unaffected: `ε` is chosen after
  the gap.

## Not formalised here

Comment **(16.24)(4)**, Example **(16.25)(2)** and the Heisenberg Theorem **(16.27)** with its
setting **(16.26)** are not in this file, nor anywhere else in the tree. Lemma **(16.28)** is in
`GibbsMeasure/Specification/BrokenShiftInvariance.lean`; the identification of the two
descriptions of `ℬ_Θ(f₁, …, f_N)` is in
`GibbsMeasure/Specification/OrderParameterSpace.lean`; the pair-potential half of Comment
**(16.24)(3)** and the gas-potential identification of Example **(16.25)(1)** are in
`GibbsMeasure/Specification/OrderParametersExamples.lean`; Example **(16.31)** is in
`GibbsMeasure/Model/AlternatingChain.lean`.

The criterion of Comment **(16.24)(3)** — that the hypothesis of Theorem (16.21)(a) holds exactly
when `1, f₁^*, …, f_N^*` are linearly independent modulo `λ`-null sets — is not proved. Its first
ingredient, the specific entropy `𝓀(α^S) = −𝓗(α | λ)` of a Bernoulli field, is
`MeasureTheory.GibbsMeasure.specificEntropy_infinitePi` in
`GibbsMeasure/Specification/OrderParametersExamples.lean`; what is missing is
`𝓗(λ(· | A) | λ) = −log λ(A)` and the linear-algebra step producing the sets `A_0, …, A_N`.
-/

